COMPONENTS BUILT INTO THE APP

The license of each component is in the "licenses" directory of the source tree and on the "Licenses" screen of the app.

crengine, the layout engine
https://github.com/koreader/crengine, commit ab1981c
Copyright (C) Vadim Lopatin and the CoolReader and KOReader contributors
GNU General Public License, used here under version 3.

Where that license comes from. The README of this fork says: "All source codes (except thirdparty directory) are provided under the terms of GNU GPL license, version 2". Its source files name no version and the tree has no license file. The upstream project, CoolReader (https://github.com/buggins/coolreader), states in its README "either version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later version", and its contributors, KOReader developers among them, agreed on "version 2 or later" in issue 338, "License collision". Perigee relies on that and uses the engine under version 3. The KOReader fork has made no statement of its own.

